    "title": "Fans are not buying Joey Porter Jr.'s excuse for missing TNF game - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Renzo Pocholo Salao ,\n1 hours ago Apr 27, 2023; Kansas City, MO, USA; Penn State cornerback Joey Porter Jr. walks the NFL Draft Red Carpet before the first round of the 2023 NFL Draft at Union Station. Mandatory Credit: Kirby Lee-USA TODAY Sports Some fans are suspicious of Joey Porter Jr. over the supposed illness that forced him to miss Thursday night’s game against the Tampa Bay Buccaneers.\nThe Dallas Cowboys cornerback was expected to make his home debut in the Week 5 clash at AT&T Stadium in Arlington, Texas. But Porter was ruled out shortly before kickoff due to an illness.\nPorter was reportedly vomiting and kept a trash can within reach to keep from redecorating the Cowboys’ locker room carpets. Fans did not buy it, with many expressing their skepticism on social media. Many felt Porter was simply upset that Dallas has yet to sign him to a new contract. Even Richard Sherman implied that Porter might have been faking it during the Amazon broadcast.\n“I think maybe if they would have gave him a new contract, maybe he would have been a little healthier today,” Sherman said before the game.\nThe Cowboys eventually sent Porter home due to the illness.\nDallas acquired Porter last week in a trade with the Pittsburgh Steelers. Porter’s relationship with the Steelers soured due to a contract dispute, leading to speculation that Porter faked a back injury to get out of playing for Pittsburgh before he was traded.\nPorter played 25 snaps in the Cowboys’ 34-30 win over the Houston Texans in Week 4 and was expected to have an even bigger role Thursday before being ruled out.\nThe post Fans are not buying Joey Porter Jr.’s excuse for missing TNF game appeared first on Larry Brown Sports .",
    "summary": "By Renzo Pocholo Salao , 1 hours ago Apr 27, 2023; Kansas City, MO, USA; Penn State cornerback Joey Porter Jr. walks the NFL Draft Red Carpet before the first round of the 2023 NFL Draft at Union Station. Mandatory Credit: Kirby Lee-USA TODAY Sports Some fans are suspicious of Joey Porter Jr. over the supposed illness that forced him to miss Thursday night’s game against the Tampa Bay Buccaneers. The Dallas Cowboys cornerback was expected to make his home debut in the Week 5 clash at AT&T Stadium in Arlington, Texas.",
